.SH "نام (NAME)"
lr_anondump \- dump database as build by lr_anonymize(1)
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBlr_anondump\fR \fIdbfile\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBlr_anondump\fR takes the name of a Berkeley DB file (e.g. /tmp/dump.email, as
build by \fBlr_anonymize\fR\|(1)) as argument, and dumps the contents of this file
to stdout. This can be useful for debugging, or in case you\*(Aqre just curious.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBlr_anonymize\fR\|(1), \fBlr_deanonymize\fR\|(1)
.SH "نسخه (VERSION)"
.IX Header "VERSION"
\&\f(CW$Id:\fR lr_anondump.in,v 1.9 2006/07/23 13:16:32 vanbaal Exp $
